; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 315. Risk assessment procedures, understanding the entity and its environment, the applicable framework and the system of internal control, identification and assessment of risks at the financial-statement and assertion levels, significant risks, stand-back and documentation.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-315\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-320\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 320: Materiality in planning and performing an audit\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-320: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 320. Materiality for the financial statements as a whole, materiality for particular classes of transactions, balances or disclosures, performance materiality, revision during the audit and documentation.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-320\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-330\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 330: The auditor's responses to assessed risks\"