for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 530. Sample design, size and selection, performing procedures, nature and cause of deviations and misstatements, projecting misstatements and evaluating results.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-530\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-540\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 540: Auditing accounting estimates and related disclosures\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-540: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 540. Risk assessment procedures for estimates, identification and assessment of risks including estimation uncertainty, responses (events after period end, testing management's process, developing a point estimate or range), disclosures, indicators of bias, overall evaluation, representations, communication and documentation.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-540\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-550\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 550: Related parties\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-550: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 550. Risk assessment procedures and related activities, identification and assessment of risks, responses to significant related-party transactions outside the normal course of business, evaluation of accounting and disclosure, representations, communication and documentation.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-550\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-560\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 560: Subsequent events\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-560: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 560. Events between the period end and the auditor's report date, facts that become known after the report date but before issue, and facts that become known after the financial statements have been issued.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-560\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-570\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 570: Going concern\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-570: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 570. Risk assessment procedures, evaluation of management's assessment, period beyond management's assessment, additional procedures when events or conditions are identified, conclusions, implications for the report, communication and delay in approval.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-570\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-580\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 580: Written representations\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-580: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 580. Management from whom representations are requested, representations about responsibilities and other representations, date and period covered, doubt as to reliability and refusal to provide representations.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-580\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-600\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 600: Special considerations: audits of group financial statements\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-600: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 600. Group engagement partner responsibilities, acceptance and continuance, overall strategy and plan, understanding the group and components, materiality, responding to assessed risks, component auditors, consolidation process, subsequent events, evaluation of evidence, communication and documentation.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-600\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-610\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 610: Using the work of internal auditors\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-610: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 610. Determining whether, in which areas and to what extent the work of the internal audit function can be used; using internal auditors to provide direct assistance; documentation.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-610\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-620\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 620: Using the work of an auditor's expert\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-620: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 620. Determining the need for an expert, nature timing and extent of procedures, competence capabilities and objectivity, understanding the field, agreement with the expert, evaluating adequacy of the expert's work, and reference in the report.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-620\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-700\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 700: Forming an opinion and reporting on financial statements\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-700: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 700. Forming the opinion, form of opinion, content and structure of the auditor's report, supplementary information.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-700\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-701\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 701: Communicating key audit matters\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-701: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 701. Determining key audit matters, communicating them in the report, communication with those charged with governance and documentation.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-701\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-705\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 705: Modifications to the opinion\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-705: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 705. Circumstances when a modification is required, determining the type of modification (qualified, adverse, disclaimer), form and content of the report when the opinion is modified, communication with those charged with governance.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-705\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-706\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 706: Emphasis of matter and other matter paragraphs\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-706: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 706. When and how to include emphasis of matter and other matter paragraphs, and communication with those charged with governance.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-706\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-710\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 710: Comparative information\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-710: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 710. Audit procedures on corresponding figures and comparative financial statements, and audit reporting for each approach.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-710\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-STD-ESA-720\",\"en\":\"Egyptian Standard on Auditing 720: The auditor's responsibilities relating to other information\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. Official Arabic text of ESA-720: SOCPA translation of the IAASB 2023-2024 Handbook (Arabic edition, available on iaasb.org behind registration) title page; and the Egyptian Standard on Auditing of the same number (Ministerial Decree 166 of 2008; 2025 standards effective 2027-01-01) for the Egyptian rendering.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Egyptian adaptation of ISA 720. Obtaining the other information, reading and considering it, responding to material inconsistencies and misstatements, reporting and documentation.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ESA-720\",\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-ASSERT-EO\",\"en\":\"Existence / occurrence\",\"ar\":\"الوجود والحدوث\",\"ar_status\":\"derived\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 3 — derived: compound of two Tier 1 assertion names\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Recorded assets, liabilities and equity interests exist at the period end, and recorded transactions and events took place and pertain to the entity. The direction of testing runs from the record to the underlying evidence: a recorded item is selected and its reality is corroborated.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ISA-315\",\"ar_tier\":3,\"derived_from\":\"[\\\"Tier 1 — IAASB 2023–2024 Handbook, Volume I, Arabic translation by SOCPA, published by IFAC (public file ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2025-04/2024 IAASB Handbook Vol 1 Arabic_0.pdf); ISA 315 (Revised 2019) paragraph A190: الوجود\\\", \\\"Tier 1 — IAASB 2023–2024 Handbook, Volume I, Arabic translation by SOCPA, published by IFAC (public file ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2025-04/2024 IAASB Handbook Vol 1 Arabic_0.pdf); ISA 315 (Revised 2019) paragraph A190: الحدوث\\\"]\"},{\"id\":\"T-ASSERT-C\",\"en\":\"Completeness\",\"ar\":\"الاكتمال\",\"ar_status\":\"sourced_isa\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 1 — IAASB 2023–2024 Handbook, Volume I, Arabic translation by SOCPA, published by IFAC (public file ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2025-04/2024 IAASB Handbook Vol 1 Arabic_0.pdf); ISA 315 (Revised 2019) paragraph A190 (assertions); occurrences confirmed in the text: 5\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Everything that should have been recorded has been recorded, and every disclosure that should have been made is included. The direction of testing runs from the underlying population to the record: an item is selected from a source outside the ledger (a shipping log, a bank statement, a contract register) and traced into the books.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ISA-315\",\"ar_tier\":1,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-ASSERT-VA\",\"en\":\"Valuation and allocation\",\"ar\":\"التقويم والتخصيص\",\"ar_status\":\"sourced_isa\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 1 — IAASB 2023–2024 Handbook, Volume I, Arabic translation by SOCPA, published by IFAC (public file ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2025-04/2024 IAASB Handbook Vol 1 Arabic_0.pdf); ISA 315 (Revised 2019) paragraph A190 (\\\"الدقة والتقويم والتخصيص\\\"); occurrences confirmed in the text: 1\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Assets, liabilities and equity interests are carried at appropriate amounts under the applicable framework, and any resulting valuation or allocation adjustments (depreciation, impairment, expected credit losses, net realisable value, fair value) are appropriately recorded. For transactions this covers accuracy: amounts and other data are recorded appropriately.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ISA-315\",\"ar_tier\":1,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-ASSERT-RO\",\"en\":\"Rights and obligations\",\"ar\":\"الحقوق والالتزامات\",\"ar_status\":\"sourced_isa\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 1 — IAASB 2023–2024 Handbook, Volume I, Arabic translation by SOCPA, published by IFAC (public file ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2025-04/2024 IAASB Handbook Vol 1 Arabic_0.pdf); ISA 315 (Revised 2019) paragraph A190 (assertions); occurrences confirmed in the text: 3\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"The entity holds or controls the rights to recorded assets, and recorded liabilities are the obligations of the entity. Legal form and economic substance are both examined: title, encumbrances, pledges, consignment and repurchase arrangements.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ISA-315\",\"ar_tier\":1,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-ASSERT-PD\",\"en\":\"Presentation and disclosure\",\"ar\":\"العرض والإفصاح\",\"ar_status\":\"sourced_isa\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 1 — IAASB 2023–2024 Handbook, Volume I, Arabic translation by SOCPA, published by IFAC (public file ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2025-04/2024 IAASB Handbook Vol 1 Arabic_0.pdf); ISA 315 (Revised 2019) paragraph A190 (العرض) and ISA 330 paragraph 24; occurrences confirmed in the text: 7\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Transactions, balances and events are appropriately aggregated or disaggregated, clearly described, and disclosed in accordance with the applicable framework; classification between current and non-current, operating and financing, and between line items is correct.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ISA-315\",\"ar_tier\":1,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-ASSERT-ACC\",\"en\":\"Accuracy\",\"ar\":\"الدقة\",\"ar_status\":\"sourced_isa\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 1 — IAASB 2023–2024 Handbook, Volume I, Arabic translation by SOCPA, published by IFAC (public file ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2025-04/2024 IAASB Handbook Vol 1 Arabic_0.pdf); ISA 315 (Revised 2019) paragraph A190 (assertions); occurrences confirmed in the text: 12\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Amounts and other data relating to recorded transactions and events have been recorded appropriately, and related disclosures are measured and described appropriately. Rolls up to valuation and allocation.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ISA-315\",\"ar_tier\":1,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-ASSERT-CO\",\"en\":\"Cut-off\",\"ar\":\"الفصل الزمني\",\"ar_status\":\"sourced_isa\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 1 — IAASB 2023–2024 Handbook, Volume I, Arabic translation by SOCPA, published by IFAC (public file ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2025-04/2024 IAASB Handbook Vol 1 Arabic_0.pdf); ISA 315 (Revised 2019) paragraph A190 (assertions); occurrences confirmed in the text: 9\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Transactions and events have been recorded in the correct accounting period. A cut-off error is simultaneously a completeness failure in one period and an occurrence failure in the adjacent period; procedures that test cut-off therefore also carry EO.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ISA-315\",\"ar_tier\":1,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-ASSERT-CL\",\"en\":\"Classification\",\"ar\":\"التصنيف\",\"ar_status\":\"sourced_isa\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 1 — IAASB 2023–2024 Handbook, Volume I, Arabic translation by SOCPA, published by IFAC (public file ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2025-04/2024 IAASB Handbook Vol 1 Arabic_0.pdf); ISA 315 (Revised 2019) paragraph A190 (assertions); occurrences confirmed in the text: 23\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Transactions and events have been recorded in the proper accounts. Rolls up to presentation and disclosure.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":\"ISA-315\",\"ar_tier\":1,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-CYCLE-REV\",\"en\":\"Revenue and receivables\",\"ar\":\"الإيرادات والمدينون\",\"ar_status\":\"derived\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 3 — derived by analogy from sourced components; compound of \\\"revenue\\\" and \\\"receivables\\\"\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Sales, contract assets and liabilities, trade receivables and the allowance for expected credit losses, credit notes and cash receipts application.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":null,\"ar_tier\":3,\"derived_from\":\"[\\\"backend/src/financial_statements.rs:IS_REVENUE = الإيرادات\\\", \\\"backend/src/financial_statements.rs:BS_AR = المدينون التجاريون\\\"]\"},{\"id\":\"T-CYCLE-PUR\",\"en\":\"Purchases, payables and expenditure\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. No ISA or ESA defines this term and the product glossary has no entry. Supply from the Egyptian Society of Accountants and Auditors terminology, the SOCPA glossary of audit terms, or a reviewer who knows Egyptian audit practice; cite the source.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Purchases of goods and services, trade and other payables, accruals, provisions and other liabilities, operating expenses and cash disbursements.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":null,\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-CYCLE-PAY\",\"en\":\"Payroll\",\"ar\":\"كشوف المرتبات\",\"ar_status\":\"existing_product\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 2 — AuditorBox reference frontend (Mercatura Forum, deployed, human-authored EN+AR): frontend/src/i18n/locales/ar.json, key documentRequests.categoryPayroll\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Wages, salaries, bonuses, social insurance, employee benefit obligations and payroll liabilities.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":null,\"ar_tier\":2,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-CYCLE-INV\",\"en\":\"Inventory and cost of sales\",\"ar\":\"المخزون وتكلفة المبيعات\",\"ar_status\":\"derived\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 3 — derived by analogy from sourced components; compound of \\\"inventory\\\" and \\\"cost of sales\\\"\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Raw materials, work in progress, finished goods, physical counts, costing, net realisable value and cost of sales.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":null,\"ar_tier\":3,\"derived_from\":\"[\\\"backend/src/financial_statements.rs:BS_INVENTORY = المخزون\\\", \\\"backend/src/financial_statements.rs:IS_COGS = تكلفة المبيعات\\\"]\"},{\"id\":\"T-CYCLE-PPE\",\"en\":\"Property, plant, equipment and intangibles\",\"ar\":\"الممتلكات والآلات والمعدات والأصول غير الملموسة\",\"ar_status\":\"derived\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 3 — derived by analogy from sourced components; compound of the two sourced leadsheet names\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Tangible and intangible non-current assets, investment property, right-of-use assets, depreciation, amortisation and impairment.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":null,\"ar_tier\":3,\"derived_from\":\"[\\\"backend/src/financial_statements.rs:BS_PPE = الممتلكات والآلات والمعدات\\\", \\\"backend/FinancialStatements.mo:BS_INTANGIBLE = الأصول غير الملموسة\\\"]\"},{\"id\":\"T-CYCLE-TRE\",\"en\":\"Treasury and financial instruments\",\"ar\":\"\",\"ar_status\":\"pending_official_source\",\"ar_source\":null,\"ar_needed\":\"Tier 1 (IFAC translations database, SOCPA, Egyptian standards) not obtainable from the authoring environment on 2026-09-09; Tier 2 (AuditorBox product glossary, chart of accounts, financial statement lines) has no entry; Tier 3 derivation not possible without sourced components. No ISA or ESA defines this term and the product glossary has no entry. Supply from the Egyptian Society of Accountants and Auditors terminology, the SOCPA glossary of audit terms, or a reviewer who knows Egyptian audit practice; cite the source.\",\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"Cash and bank, borrowings, lease liabilities, investments, derivatives, finance income and costs, and covenant compliance.\",\"definition_ar\":null,\"definition_ar_status\":\"pending_draft\",\"standard_id\":null,\"ar_tier\":null,\"derived_from\":null},{\"id\":\"T-CYCLE-EQY\",\"en\":\"Equity\",\"ar\":\"المصروفات\",\"ar_status\":\"existing_product\",\"ar_source\":\"Tier 2 — AuditorBox reference frontend (Mercatura Forum, deployed, human-authored EN+AR): frontend/src/data/egyptianChartOfAccounts.ts, key comment (Equity)\",\"ar_needed\":null,\"ar_alt\":null,\"ar_alt_source\":null,\"definition_en\":\"